title: Marko Virtual
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/marko-virtual"},{"type":"text","value":" is the Marko 6 adapter for TanStack Virtual. It provides\nrow, column, and grid virtualisation via two auto-discovered Marko tags:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — element-based scrolling (rows, columns, grids)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<window-virtualizer>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — full-page/window scrolling"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tags are discovered automatically by the Marko compiler when the package is\ninstalled. No imports are needed in your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".marko"},{"type":"text","value":" files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each tag is used "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"self-closing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and exposes a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tag variable"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (written "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer/v/>"},{"type":"text","value":").\nYou then own the markup, reading "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v.virtualItems"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v.totalSize"},{"type":"text","value":" to render the visible rows."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/marko-virtual","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"row-virtualisation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row virtualisation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"height: 400px; width: 400px; overflow-y: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; width: 100%; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div\n        style=`\n          position: absolute;\n          top: 0;\n          left: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: ${item.size}px;\n          transform: translateY(${item.start}px);\n        `\n      >\n        Row ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-virtualisation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column virtualisation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same tag, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"horizontal=true"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"width: 400px; height: 100px; overflow-x: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 100\n    horizontal=true\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`width: ${v.totalSize}px; height: 100%; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div\n        style=`\n          position: absolute;\n          top: 0;\n          left: 0;\n          height: 100%;\n          width: ${item.size}px;\n          transform: translateX(${item.start}px);\n        `\n      >\n        Column ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grid-virtualisation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grid virtualisation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compose two "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" tags — one for rows, one for columns — sharing the\nsame scroll element. Each returns its own tag variable. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getScrollElement"},{"type":"text","value":" as an\narrow ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => ref()"},{"type":"text","value":") so each virtualizer resolves its own element:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"height: 500px; width: 500px; overflow: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/rowV\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <virtualizer/colV\n    count=200\n    estimateSize=() => 100\n    horizontal=true\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${rowV.totalSize}px; width: ${colV.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|row| of=rowV.virtualItems>\n      <for|col| of=colV.virtualItems>\n        <div\n          style=`\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            width: ${col.size}px;\n            height: ${row.size}px;\n            transform: translateX(${col.start}px) translateY(${row.start}px);\n          `\n        >\n          Cell ${row.index}, ${col.index}\n        </div>\n      </for>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"window-virtualisation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Window virtualisation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<window-virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" when the entire page scrolls rather than a container:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<window-virtualizer/v\n  count=10000\n  estimateSize=() => 35\n/>\n<div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n  <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n    <div\n      style=`\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 0;\n        left: 0;\n        width: 100%;\n        height: ${item.size}px;\n        transform: translateY(${item.start}px);\n      `\n    >\n      Row ${item.index}\n    </div>\n  </for>\n</div>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"dynamic-variable-item-sizes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic / variable item sizes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For items with unknown heights, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureElement"},{"type":"text","value":" as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":"-driven ref\nto measure each element after render:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div/scrollEl style=\"height: 400px; overflow-y: auto\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=data.length\n    estimateSize=() => 50\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div/el\n        data-index=item.index\n        style=`position: absolute; top: 0; width: 100%; transform: translateY(${item.start}px)`>\n        <script() {\n          // re-run when the item changes; measureElement reads the rendered\n          // height and feeds it back to the virtualizer\n          const _key = item.key\n          if (el() && v.measureElement) v.measureElement(el())\n        }/>\n        ${data[item.index].text}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tag-variable-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tag variable reference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both tags are self-closing and expose the same tag-variable shape. Capture it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer/v/>"},{"type":"text","value":" (or any name) and read its properties as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v.property"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"virtualItems"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VirtualItem[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The currently visible virtual items"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"totalSize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Total scrollable size in px — set as the inner container's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" for columns)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"range"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ startIndex: number; endIndex: number } | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The visible index window (excludes overscan). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" until there is a window. Useful for deriving things like the active sticky header"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureElement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(el: Element | null) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ref callback for dynamic item sizing"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollToIndex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(index: number, options?: ScrollToOptions) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Imperatively scroll to an item by index. Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"align: 'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":" scrolls the MINIMUM: downward jumps land the item at the viewport end, upward jumps align it to the start (below "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollPaddingStart"},{"type":"text","value":"), and an already fully visible item does not move. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ align: 'start' }"},{"type":"text","value":" to always align to the start"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollToOffset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(offset: number, options?: ScrollToOptions) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Imperatively scroll to a pixel offset"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measure"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drop all measured sizes and re-measure everything (after a width/font change)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resizeItem"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(index: number, size: number) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set one item's size directly, without a DOM measure"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollToEnd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(options?: { behavior?: ScrollBehavior }) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scroll to the very end of the list"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isAtEnd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(threshold?: number) => boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether the scroll position is at (or within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threshold"},{"type":"text","value":" px of) the end. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" before mount"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getDistanceFromEnd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pixels between the current scroll position and the end. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" before mount"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"virtualizer-input-reference","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" input reference"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"count"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Number of items"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getScrollElement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => Element | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the scroll container"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"estimateSize"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(index: number) => number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => 50"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Estimated item size in px"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overscan"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Items to render beyond the visible area"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"horizontal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Virtualise horizontally (columns)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paddingStart"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Padding before first item"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paddingEnd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Padding after last item"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollPaddingStart"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scroll padding for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollToIndex"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollPaddingEnd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scroll padding for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollToIndex"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gap"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gap between items in px"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lanes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lanes for masonry layouts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialOffset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | (() => number)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scroll offset (px) for the server slice — server-render at a scroll position (deep link / restore). Element only; see "},{"type":"link","href":"#ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR"}]}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialRect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ width: number; height: number }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Viewport hint for a server-rendered slice (SSR). When set, the server paints the initial visible rows; omit for client-only fill. See "},{"type":"link","href":"#ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getItemKey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(index: number) => number | string | bigint"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the index"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable per-item identity so cached measurements survive reorder"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rangeExtractor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(range: Range) => number[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultRangeExtractor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook over the visible range: force extra indexes (e.g. a pinned sticky header) into the rendered window. Compose with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultRangeExtractor"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/virtual-core"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"indexAttribute"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'data-index'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DOM attribute carrying the item index for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureElement"},{"type":"text","value":". Give two instances measuring the same element (a grid cell) distinct attributes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialMeasurementsCache"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VirtualItem[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-measured items (plain data) to seed the measurement cache"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anchorTo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'start' | 'end'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'start'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anchor the window to the list end (a chat pinned to newest). Client-behavioral: it does not position the server slice — use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialOffset"},{"type":"text","value":" for that"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"followOnAppend"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean | ScrollBehavior"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anchorTo=\"end\""},{"type":"text","value":": stay pinned to the end as items append"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollEndThreshold"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How close (px) to the end still counts as \"at the end\""}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollMargin"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The list's offset (px) from the top of its scroll area, when other content sits above it in the same scroller. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item.start"},{"type":"text","value":" values then INCLUDE this margin — subtract it when positioning items relative to the list (see the window example)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable switch. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" is not a freeze: the virtualizer unobserves, clears its measurements, and renders an empty window until re-enabled"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRtl"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Right-to-left horizontal lists"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isScrollingResetDelay"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"150"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ms after the last scroll event before \"user is scrolling\" ends"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useScrollendEvent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollend"},{"type":"text","value":" event instead of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isScrollingResetDelay"},{"type":"text","value":" timer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAnimationFrameWithResizeObserver"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Batch ResizeObserver measurements into animation frames (avoids \"ResizeObserver loop\" console errors under heavy resize load)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laneAssignmentMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'estimate' | 'measured'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'estimate'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Masonry/multi-lane: assign items to lanes by estimated or measured sizes"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useCachedMeasurements"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Make the default measurer return the cached (or estimated) size instead of reading the DOM — freezes item sizes when they are already known"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debug"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verbose engine logging"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureElement"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(element, entry, instance) => number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"border-box measurer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace HOW an item's size is read from its element (e.g. include margins, or measure a child)"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"window-virtualizer-input-reference","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<window-virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" input reference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" except "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getScrollElement"},{"type":"text","value":" is not accepted — the scroll element is\nalways "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window"},{"type":"text","value":". Unlike "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" there are two changed defaults:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"horizontal"},{"type":"text","value":" is accepted (the page scrolls sideways) and defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialOffset"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to the live window scroll position ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.scrollY"},{"type":"text","value":", or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.scrollX"},{"type":"text","value":" when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"horizontal"},{"type":"text","value":") on the client and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server. Pass a number to\noverride it — e.g. to server-render a slice at a scroll position, paired with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialRect"},{"type":"text","value":" (see "},{"type":"link","href":"#ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollMargin"},{"type":"text","value":" is the signature window-virtualizer option: a window-scrolled list almost never\nstarts at the very top of the page, so pass the list's offset from the top of the document and\nsubtract it from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item.start"},{"type":"text","value":" when positioning (the window example measures it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"offsetTop"},{"type":"text","value":" on mount)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"inside-your-own-scroll-handler-read-the-element-not-the-virtualizer","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inside your own scroll handler, read the element — not the virtualizer"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The virtualizer attaches its scroll listener in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMount"},{"type":"text","value":"; a handler in your markup attaches\nat hydrate, earlier. During any single scroll event your handler therefore runs FIRST, while\nthe virtualizer still holds the PREVIOUS event's offset — so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v.isAtEnd()"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v.getDistanceFromEnd()"},{"type":"text","value":" called inside your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onScroll"},{"type":"text","value":" are one event stale (a jump to the top\ncan still report \"at end\"). Compute from the element instead; the arithmetic is identical:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div/scrollEl onScroll() {\n  const el = scrollEl()\n  if (!el) return\n  const atEnd = el.scrollHeight - el.scrollTop - el.clientHeight <= 80\n}>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Everywhere else — click handlers, effects, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" blocks — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v.isAtEnd()"},{"type":"text","value":" and friends are\ncurrent and safe to use."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-virtualizer-s-lifetime-must-match-its-scroll-element-s","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The virtualizer's lifetime must match its scroll element's"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Declare the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" in the same conditional scope as its scroll element. If the\nscroll container can be unmounted and remounted (an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<if>"},{"type":"text","value":", a route transition), put the\ntag inside that same conditional:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<if=show>\n  <virtualizer/v count=1000 estimateSize=() => 35 getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()/>\n  <div/scrollEl class=\"list\">...</div>\n</if>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tag builds its live virtualizer in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMount"},{"type":"text","value":" and re-reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getScrollElement"},{"type":"text","value":" only when\none of its inputs changes. A scroll element replaced WITHOUT any input change is invisible\nto the tag — Marko's compile-time reactivity cannot track through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getScrollElement"},{"type":"text","value":"\nthunk into your template's scope — so a tag left mounted outside the conditional would stay\nbound to the removed element and render nothing after the remount. Co-locating the tag makes\nits lifecycle follow the element's: unmount tears the instance down, remount builds a fresh\none. (Note: scroll position resets on remount, as a fresh element starts at offset 0.)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both tags render on the server "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"without an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<if=mounted>"},{"type":"text","value":" guard"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and build their live, observing\nvirtualizer client-side in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMount"},{"type":"text","value":". There are two modes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-fill (default)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialRect"},{"type":"text","value":" the server renders an empty container; on mount the\nclient measures the scroll element and fills in the visible rows:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div/scrollEl style=\"height: 400px; overflow-y: auto; position: relative;\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div style=`position: absolute; top: 0; width: 100%; height: ${item.size}px; transform: translateY(${item.start}px)`>\n        Row ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server slice ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialRect"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Pass a viewport hint and the server paints the initial visible\nrows into the HTML, so there is real content on first paint before the client resumes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<virtualizer/v\n  count=people.length\n  estimateSize=() => 48\n  getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n/>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialRect"},{"type":"text","value":" is a hint, not a measurement: the server has no real viewport, so it uses this size to\ncompute the slice, and the client re-measures the actual scroll element on mount and takes over. The\ninstance built for the slice is transient — nothing live is serialized; only plain data (the item\npositions and total size) crosses and recomputes identically on resume. The full\nfetch → serialize → resume → slice flow is shown in the SSR data-fetching example."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note (no-JS):"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a server slice does not by itself make a no-JavaScript page. If the virtualizer\nsits inside an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<await>"},{"type":"text","value":" with a placeholder (as in the data-fetching examples), Marko streams the\nawaited content out of order and reveals it with a small inline script — with JavaScript disabled\nthe painted rows are in the HTML but the page renders blank. Script-free visibility requires\nin-order rendering (no placeholder)."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scroll restore ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialOffset"},{"type":"text","value":", element only)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" To server-render the list at a scroll position\ninstead of the top — a deep link, or a restored scroll — pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialOffset"},{"type":"text","value":" alongside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialRect"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe server paints the slice around that offset (it includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overscan"},{"type":"text","value":", so the first "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"painted"}]},{"type":"text","value":" row\nsits a few rows above the first "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"visible"}]},{"type":"text","value":" one). A scroll container's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollTop"},{"type":"text","value":" can't be set\ndeclaratively in HTML, so restore it on the client on mount to line the rows up:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div/scrollEl class=\"list\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=people.length\n    estimateSize=() => 48\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n    initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n    initialOffset=(100 * 48)\n  />\n  <!-- rows … -->\n</div>\n<lifecycle onMount() { const el = scrollEl(); if (el) el.scrollTop = 100 * 48 }/>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<window-virtualizer>"},{"type":"text","value":" the offset comes from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.scrollY"},{"type":"text","value":" (browser scroll restoration), so\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialOffset"},{"type":"text","value":" is not a separate prop there."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"streaming-the-tag-inside-await","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming: the tag inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<await>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The SSR modes above compose with Marko's streaming as-is — place the virtualizer inside an\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<await>"},{"type":"text","value":" and everything holds "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"per streamed chunk"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<try>\n  <@placeholder>\n    <p>Loading people…</p>\n  </@placeholder>\n  <@catch|err|>\n    <p>Failed to load: ${(err as Error).message}</p>\n  </@catch>\n\n  <await|people| value=fetchPeople()>\n    <div/scrollEl class=\"scroll-container\">\n      <virtualizer/v\n        count=people.length\n        estimateSize=() => 48\n        getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n        initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n      />\n      <!-- sizer + rows exactly as usual -->\n    </div>\n  </await>\n</try>","lang":"marko"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the wire, the server flushes the page shell (with the placeholder) immediately and streams the\nawaited subtree as a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"later chunk"}]},{"type":"text","value":" once "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchPeople()"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves — including the server-painted\nrows when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialRect"},{"type":"text","value":" is set. Each streamed chunk "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resumes independently"}]},{"type":"text","value":": this list's live\nvirtualizer mounts when its chunk arrives, without waiting for the rest of the page. No extra\nconfiguration — the slice is computed inside the awaited subtree from the resolved data, so the\nserver and the resumed client agree by construction. (The no-JS note above applies: streamed\ncontent is revealed by script.)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The SSR data-fetching example shows the streamed pattern with client-rendered rows; the\nserver-slice example shows it with server-painted rows — its test suite includes a wire-level\nassertion that the placeholder flushes first and the painted rows arrive in a later chunk."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"row-virtualisation","text":"Row virtualisation","level":2},{"id":"column-virtualisation","text":"Column virtualisation","level":2},{"id":"grid-virtualisation","text":"Grid virtualisation","level":2},{"id":"window-virtualisation","text":"Window virtualisation","level":2},{"id":"dynamic-variable-item-sizes","text":"Dynamic / variable item sizes","level":2},{"id":"tag-variable-reference","text":"Tag variable reference","level":2},{"id":"virtualizer-input-reference","text":"<virtualizer> input reference","level":2},{"id":"window-virtualizer-input-reference","text":"<window-virtualizer> input reference","level":2},{"id":"inside-your-own-scroll-handler-read-the-element-not-the-virtualizer","text":"Inside your own scroll handler, read the element — not the virtualizer","level":2},{"id":"the-virtualizer-s-lifetime-must-match-its-scroll-element-s","text":"The virtualizer's lifetime must match its scroll element's","level":2},{"id":"ssr","text":"SSR","level":2},{"id":"streaming-the-tag-inside-await","text":"Streaming: the tag inside <await>","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`@tanstack/marko-virtual` is the Marko 6 adapter for TanStack Virtual. It provides\nrow, column, and grid virtualisation via two auto-discovered Marko tags:\n\n- **`<virtualizer>`** — element-based scrolling (rows, columns, grids)\n- **`<window-virtualizer>`** — full-page/window scrolling\n\nTags are discovered automatically by the Marko compiler when the package is\ninstalled. No imports are needed in your `.marko` files.\n\nEach tag is used **self-closing** and exposes a **tag variable** (written `<virtualizer/v/>`).\nYou then own the markup, reading `v.virtualItems` and `v.totalSize` to render the visible rows.\n\n## Installation\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/marko-virtual\n```\n\n## Row virtualisation\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"height: 400px; width: 400px; overflow-y: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; width: 100%; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div\n        style=`\n          position: absolute;\n          top: 0;\n          left: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: ${item.size}px;\n          transform: translateY(${item.start}px);\n        `\n      >\n        Row ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Column virtualisation\n\nSame tag, `horizontal=true`:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"width: 400px; height: 100px; overflow-x: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 100\n    horizontal=true\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`width: ${v.totalSize}px; height: 100%; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div\n        style=`\n          position: absolute;\n          top: 0;\n          left: 0;\n          height: 100%;\n          width: ${item.size}px;\n          transform: translateX(${item.start}px);\n        `\n      >\n        Column ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Grid virtualisation\n\nCompose two `<virtualizer>` tags — one for rows, one for columns — sharing the\nsame scroll element. Each returns its own tag variable. Pass `getScrollElement` as an\narrow (`() => ref()`) so each virtualizer resolves its own element:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"height: 500px; width: 500px; overflow: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/rowV\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <virtualizer/colV\n    count=200\n    estimateSize=() => 100\n    horizontal=true\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${rowV.totalSize}px; width: ${colV.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|row| of=rowV.virtualItems>\n      <for|col| of=colV.virtualItems>\n        <div\n          style=`\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            width: ${col.size}px;\n            height: ${row.size}px;\n            transform: translateX(${col.start}px) translateY(${row.start}px);\n          `\n        >\n          Cell ${row.index}, ${col.index}\n        </div>\n      </for>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Window virtualisation\n\nUse `<window-virtualizer>` when the entire page scrolls rather than a container:\n\n```marko\n<window-virtualizer/v\n  count=10000\n  estimateSize=() => 35\n/>\n<div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n  <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n    <div\n      style=`\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 0;\n        left: 0;\n        width: 100%;\n        height: ${item.size}px;\n        transform: translateY(${item.start}px);\n      `\n    >\n      Row ${item.index}\n    </div>\n  </for>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Dynamic / variable item sizes\n\nFor items with unknown heights, use `measureElement` as a `<script>`-driven ref\nto measure each element after render:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl style=\"height: 400px; overflow-y: auto\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=data.length\n    estimateSize=() => 50\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div/el\n        data-index=item.index\n        style=`position: absolute; top: 0; width: 100%; transform: translateY(${item.start}px)`>\n        <script() {\n          // re-run when the item changes; measureElement reads the rendered\n          // height and feeds it back to the virtualizer\n          const _key = item.key\n          if (el() && v.measureElement) v.measureElement(el())\n        }/>\n        ${data[item.index].text}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Tag variable reference\n\nBoth tags are self-closing and expose the same tag-variable shape. Capture it with\n`<virtualizer/v/>` (or any name) and read its properties as `v.property`:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `virtualItems` | `VirtualItem[]` | The currently visible virtual items |\n| `totalSize` | `number` | Total scrollable size in px — set as the inner container's `height` (or `width` for columns) |\n| `range` | `{ startIndex: number; endIndex: number } \\| null` | The visible index window (excludes overscan). `null` until there is a window. Useful for deriving things like the active sticky header |\n| `measureElement` | `(el: Element \\| null) => void` | Ref callback for dynamic item sizing |\n| `scrollToIndex` | `(index: number, options?: ScrollToOptions) => void` | Imperatively scroll to an item by index. Default `align: 'auto'` scrolls the MINIMUM: downward jumps land the item at the viewport end, upward jumps align it to the start (below `scrollPaddingStart`), and an already fully visible item does not move. Pass `{ align: 'start' }` to always align to the start |\n| `scrollToOffset` | `(offset: number, options?: ScrollToOptions) => void` | Imperatively scroll to a pixel offset |\n| `measure` | `() => void` | Drop all measured sizes and re-measure everything (after a width/font change) |\n| `resizeItem` | `(index: number, size: number) => void` | Set one item's size directly, without a DOM measure |\n| `scrollToEnd` | `(options?: { behavior?: ScrollBehavior }) => void` | Scroll to the very end of the list |\n| `isAtEnd` | `(threshold?: number) => boolean` | Whether the scroll position is at (or within `threshold` px of) the end. `false` before mount |\n| `getDistanceFromEnd` | `() => number` | Pixels between the current scroll position and the end. `Infinity` before mount |\n\n## `<virtualizer>` input reference\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `count` | `number` | required | Number of items |\n| `getScrollElement` | `() => Element \\| null` | required | Returns the scroll container |\n| `estimateSize` | `(index: number) => number` | `() => 50` | Estimated item size in px |\n| `overscan` | `number` | `5` | Items to render beyond the visible area |\n| `horizontal` | `boolean` | `false` | Virtualise horizontally (columns) |\n| `paddingStart` | `number` | — | Padding before first item |\n| `paddingEnd` | `number` | — | Padding after last item |\n| `scrollPaddingStart` | `number` | — | Scroll padding for `scrollToIndex` |\n| `scrollPaddingEnd` | `number` | — | Scroll padding for `scrollToIndex` |\n| `gap` | `number` | — | Gap between items in px |\n| `lanes` | `number` | `1` | Lanes for masonry layouts |\n| `initialOffset` | `number \\| (() => number)` | — | Scroll offset (px) for the server slice — server-render at a scroll position (deep link / restore). Element only; see [SSR](#ssr) |\n| `initialRect` | `{ width: number; height: number }` | — | Viewport hint for a server-rendered slice (SSR). When set, the server paints the initial visible rows; omit for client-only fill. See [SSR](#ssr). |\n| `getItemKey` | `(index: number) => number \\| string \\| bigint` | the index | Stable per-item identity so cached measurements survive reorder |\n| `rangeExtractor` | `(range: Range) => number[]` | `defaultRangeExtractor` | Hook over the visible range: force extra indexes (e.g. a pinned sticky header) into the rendered window. Compose with `defaultRangeExtractor` from `@tanstack/virtual-core` |\n| `indexAttribute` | `string` | `'data-index'` | DOM attribute carrying the item index for `measureElement`. Give two instances measuring the same element (a grid cell) distinct attributes |\n| `initialMeasurementsCache` | `VirtualItem[]` | — | Pre-measured items (plain data) to seed the measurement cache |\n| `anchorTo` | `'start' \\| 'end'` | `'start'` | Anchor the window to the list end (a chat pinned to newest). Client-behavioral: it does not position the server slice — use `initialOffset` for that |\n| `followOnAppend` | `boolean \\| ScrollBehavior` | `false` | With `anchorTo=\"end\"`: stay pinned to the end as items append |\n| `scrollEndThreshold` | `number` | `1` | How close (px) to the end still counts as \"at the end\" |\n| `scrollMargin` | `number` | `0` | The list's offset (px) from the top of its scroll area, when other content sits above it in the same scroller. `item.start` values then INCLUDE this margin — subtract it when positioning items relative to the list (see the window example) |\n| `enabled` | `boolean` | `true` | Disable switch. `false` is not a freeze: the virtualizer unobserves, clears its measurements, and renders an empty window until re-enabled |\n| `isRtl` | `boolean` | `false` | Right-to-left horizontal lists |\n| `isScrollingResetDelay` | `number` | `150` | ms after the last scroll event before \"user is scrolling\" ends |\n| `useScrollendEvent` | `boolean` | `false` | Use the native `scrollend` event instead of the `isScrollingResetDelay` timer |\n| `useAnimationFrameWithResizeObserver` | `boolean` | `false` | Batch ResizeObserver measurements into animation frames (avoids \"ResizeObserver loop\" console errors under heavy resize load) |\n| `laneAssignmentMode` | `'estimate' \\| 'measured'` | `'estimate'` | Masonry/multi-lane: assign items to lanes by estimated or measured sizes |\n| `useCachedMeasurements` | `boolean` | `false` | Make the default measurer return the cached (or estimated) size instead of reading the DOM — freezes item sizes when they are already known |\n| `debug` | `boolean` | `false` | Verbose engine logging |\n| `measureElement` | `(element, entry, instance) => number` | border-box measurer | Replace HOW an item's size is read from its element (e.g. include margins, or measure a child) |\n\n## `<window-virtualizer>` input reference\n\nSame as `<virtualizer>` except `getScrollElement` is not accepted — the scroll element is\nalways `window`. Unlike `<virtualizer>` there are two changed defaults:\n\n- `horizontal` is accepted (the page scrolls sideways) and defaults to `false`.\n- `initialOffset` defaults to the live window scroll position (`window.scrollY`, or\n  `window.scrollX` when `horizontal`) on the client and `0` on the server. Pass a number to\n  override it — e.g. to server-render a slice at a scroll position, paired with\n  `initialRect` (see [SSR](#ssr)).\n\n`scrollMargin` is the signature window-virtualizer option: a window-scrolled list almost never\nstarts at the very top of the page, so pass the list's offset from the top of the document and\nsubtract it from `item.start` when positioning (the window example measures it with\n`offsetTop` on mount).\n\n## Inside your own scroll handler, read the element — not the virtualizer\n\nThe virtualizer attaches its scroll listener in `onMount`; a handler in your markup attaches\nat hydrate, earlier. During any single scroll event your handler therefore runs FIRST, while\nthe virtualizer still holds the PREVIOUS event's offset — so `v.isAtEnd()` and\n`v.getDistanceFromEnd()` called inside your `onScroll` are one event stale (a jump to the top\ncan still report \"at end\"). Compute from the element instead; the arithmetic is identical:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl onScroll() {\n  const el = scrollEl()\n  if (!el) return\n  const atEnd = el.scrollHeight - el.scrollTop - el.clientHeight <= 80\n}>\n```\n\nEverywhere else — click handlers, effects, `<script>` blocks — `v.isAtEnd()` and friends are\ncurrent and safe to use.\n\n## The virtualizer's lifetime must match its scroll element's\n\nDeclare the `<virtualizer>` in the same conditional scope as its scroll element. If the\nscroll container can be unmounted and remounted (an `<if>`, a route transition), put the\ntag inside that same conditional:\n\n```marko\n<if=show>\n  <virtualizer/v count=1000 estimateSize=() => 35 getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()/>\n  <div/scrollEl class=\"list\">...</div>\n</if>\n```\n\nThe tag builds its live virtualizer in `onMount` and re-reads `getScrollElement` only when\none of its inputs changes. A scroll element replaced WITHOUT any input change is invisible\nto the tag — Marko's compile-time reactivity cannot track through the `getScrollElement`\nthunk into your template's scope — so a tag left mounted outside the conditional would stay\nbound to the removed element and render nothing after the remount. Co-locating the tag makes\nits lifecycle follow the element's: unmount tears the instance down, remount builds a fresh\none. (Note: scroll position resets on remount, as a fresh element starts at offset 0.)\n\n## SSR\n\nBoth tags render on the server **without an `<if=mounted>` guard** and build their live, observing\nvirtualizer client-side in `onMount`. There are two modes.\n\n**Client-fill (default).** Without `initialRect` the server renders an empty container; on mount the\nclient measures the scroll element and fills in the visible rows:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl style=\"height: 400px; overflow-y: auto; position: relative;\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div style=`position: absolute; top: 0; width: 100%; height: ${item.size}px; transform: translateY(${item.start}px)`>\n        Row ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n**Server slice (`initialRect`).** Pass a viewport hint and the server paints the initial visible\nrows into the HTML, so there is real content on first paint before the client resumes:\n\n```marko\n<virtualizer/v\n  count=people.length\n  estimateSize=() => 48\n  getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n/>\n```\n\n`initialRect` is a hint, not a measurement: the server has no real viewport, so it uses this size to\ncompute the slice, and the client re-measures the actual scroll element on mount and takes over. The\ninstance built for the slice is transient — nothing live is serialized; only plain data (the item\npositions and total size) crosses and recomputes identically on resume. The full\nfetch → serialize → resume → slice flow is shown in the SSR data-fetching example.\n\n> **Note (no-JS):** a server slice does not by itself make a no-JavaScript page. If the virtualizer\n> sits inside an `<await>` with a placeholder (as in the data-fetching examples), Marko streams the\n> awaited content out of order and reveals it with a small inline script — with JavaScript disabled\n> the painted rows are in the HTML but the page renders blank. Script-free visibility requires\n> in-order rendering (no placeholder).\n\n**Scroll restore (`initialOffset`, element only).** To server-render the list at a scroll position\ninstead of the top — a deep link, or a restored scroll — pass `initialOffset` alongside `initialRect`.\nThe server paints the slice around that offset (it includes `overscan`, so the first *painted* row\nsits a few rows above the first *visible* one). A scroll container's `scrollTop` can't be set\ndeclaratively in HTML, so restore it on the client on mount to line the rows up:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl class=\"list\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=people.length\n    estimateSize=() => 48\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n    initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n    initialOffset=(100 * 48)\n  />\n  <!-- rows … -->\n</div>\n<lifecycle onMount() { const el = scrollEl(); if (el) el.scrollTop = 100 * 48 }/>\n```\n\nFor `<window-virtualizer>` the offset comes from `window.scrollY` (browser scroll restoration), so\n`initialOffset` is not a separate prop there.\n\n### Streaming: the tag inside `<await>`\n\nThe SSR modes above compose with Marko's streaming as-is — place the virtualizer inside an\n`<await>` and everything holds *per streamed chunk*:\n\n```marko\n<try>\n  <@placeholder>\n    <p>Loading people…</p>\n  </@placeholder>\n  <@catch|err|>\n    <p>Failed to load: ${(err as Error).message}</p>\n  </@catch>\n\n  <await|people| value=fetchPeople()>\n    <div/scrollEl class=\"scroll-container\">\n      <virtualizer/v\n        count=people.length\n        estimateSize=() => 48\n        getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n        initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n      />\n      <!-- sizer + rows exactly as usual -->\n    </div>\n  </await>\n</try>\n```\n\nOn the wire, the server flushes the page shell (with the placeholder) immediately and streams the\nawaited subtree as a **later chunk** once `fetchPeople()` resolves — including the server-painted\nrows when `initialRect` is set. Each streamed chunk **resumes independently**: this list's live\nvirtualizer mounts when its chunk arrives, without waiting for the rest of the page. No extra\nconfiguration — the slice is computed inside the awaited subtree from the resolved data, so the\nserver and the resumed client agree by construction. (The no-JS note above applies: streamed\ncontent is revealed by script.)\n\nThe SSR data-fetching example shows the streamed pattern with client-rendered rows; the\nserver-slice example shows it with server-painted rows — its test suite includes a wire-level\nassertion that the placeholder flushes first and the painted rows arrive in a later chunk.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Marko Virtual\n---\n\n`@tanstack/marko-virtual` is the Marko 6 adapter for TanStack Virtual. It provides\nrow, column, and grid virtualisation via two auto-discovered Marko tags:\n\n- **`<virtualizer>`** — element-based scrolling (rows, columns, grids)\n- **`<window-virtualizer>`** — full-page/window scrolling\n\nTags are discovered automatically by the Marko compiler when the package is\ninstalled. No imports are needed in your `.marko` files.\n\nEach tag is used **self-closing** and exposes a **tag variable** (written `<virtualizer/v/>`).\nYou then own the markup, reading `v.virtualItems` and `v.totalSize` to render the visible rows.\n\n## Installation\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/marko-virtual\n```\n\n## Row virtualisation\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"height: 400px; width: 400px; overflow-y: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; width: 100%; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div\n        style=`\n          position: absolute;\n          top: 0;\n          left: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: ${item.size}px;\n          transform: translateY(${item.start}px);\n        `\n      >\n        Row ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Column virtualisation\n\nSame tag, `horizontal=true`:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"width: 400px; height: 100px; overflow-x: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 100\n    horizontal=true\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`width: ${v.totalSize}px; height: 100%; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div\n        style=`\n          position: absolute;\n          top: 0;\n          left: 0;\n          height: 100%;\n          width: ${item.size}px;\n          transform: translateX(${item.start}px);\n        `\n      >\n        Column ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Grid virtualisation\n\nCompose two `<virtualizer>` tags — one for rows, one for columns — sharing the\nsame scroll element. Each returns its own tag variable. Pass `getScrollElement` as an\narrow (`() => ref()`) so each virtualizer resolves its own element:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl\n  style=\"height: 500px; width: 500px; overflow: auto; position: relative;\"\n>\n  <virtualizer/rowV\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <virtualizer/colV\n    count=200\n    estimateSize=() => 100\n    horizontal=true\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${rowV.totalSize}px; width: ${colV.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|row| of=rowV.virtualItems>\n      <for|col| of=colV.virtualItems>\n        <div\n          style=`\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            width: ${col.size}px;\n            height: ${row.size}px;\n            transform: translateX(${col.start}px) translateY(${row.start}px);\n          `\n        >\n          Cell ${row.index}, ${col.index}\n        </div>\n      </for>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Window virtualisation\n\nUse `<window-virtualizer>` when the entire page scrolls rather than a container:\n\n```marko\n<window-virtualizer/v\n  count=10000\n  estimateSize=() => 35\n/>\n<div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n  <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n    <div\n      style=`\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 0;\n        left: 0;\n        width: 100%;\n        height: ${item.size}px;\n        transform: translateY(${item.start}px);\n      `\n    >\n      Row ${item.index}\n    </div>\n  </for>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Dynamic / variable item sizes\n\nFor items with unknown heights, use `measureElement` as a `<script>`-driven ref\nto measure each element after render:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl style=\"height: 400px; overflow-y: auto\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=data.length\n    estimateSize=() => 50\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div/el\n        data-index=item.index\n        style=`position: absolute; top: 0; width: 100%; transform: translateY(${item.start}px)`>\n        <script() {\n          // re-run when the item changes; measureElement reads the rendered\n          // height and feeds it back to the virtualizer\n          const _key = item.key\n          if (el() && v.measureElement) v.measureElement(el())\n        }/>\n        ${data[item.index].text}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Tag variable reference\n\nBoth tags are self-closing and expose the same tag-variable shape. Capture it with\n`<virtualizer/v/>` (or any name) and read its properties as `v.property`:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `virtualItems` | `VirtualItem[]` | The currently visible virtual items |\n| `totalSize` | `number` | Total scrollable size in px — set as the inner container's `height` (or `width` for columns) |\n| `range` | `{ startIndex: number; endIndex: number } \\| null` | The visible index window (excludes overscan). `null` until there is a window. Useful for deriving things like the active sticky header |\n| `measureElement` | `(el: Element \\| null) => void` | Ref callback for dynamic item sizing |\n| `scrollToIndex` | `(index: number, options?: ScrollToOptions) => void` | Imperatively scroll to an item by index. Default `align: 'auto'` scrolls the MINIMUM: downward jumps land the item at the viewport end, upward jumps align it to the start (below `scrollPaddingStart`), and an already fully visible item does not move. Pass `{ align: 'start' }` to always align to the start |\n| `scrollToOffset` | `(offset: number, options?: ScrollToOptions) => void` | Imperatively scroll to a pixel offset |\n| `measure` | `() => void` | Drop all measured sizes and re-measure everything (after a width/font change) |\n| `resizeItem` | `(index: number, size: number) => void` | Set one item's size directly, without a DOM measure |\n| `scrollToEnd` | `(options?: { behavior?: ScrollBehavior }) => void` | Scroll to the very end of the list |\n| `isAtEnd` | `(threshold?: number) => boolean` | Whether the scroll position is at (or within `threshold` px of) the end. `false` before mount |\n| `getDistanceFromEnd` | `() => number` | Pixels between the current scroll position and the end. `Infinity` before mount |\n\n## `<virtualizer>` input reference\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `count` | `number` | required | Number of items |\n| `getScrollElement` | `() => Element \\| null` | required | Returns the scroll container |\n| `estimateSize` | `(index: number) => number` | `() => 50` | Estimated item size in px |\n| `overscan` | `number` | `5` | Items to render beyond the visible area |\n| `horizontal` | `boolean` | `false` | Virtualise horizontally (columns) |\n| `paddingStart` | `number` | — | Padding before first item |\n| `paddingEnd` | `number` | — | Padding after last item |\n| `scrollPaddingStart` | `number` | — | Scroll padding for `scrollToIndex` |\n| `scrollPaddingEnd` | `number` | — | Scroll padding for `scrollToIndex` |\n| `gap` | `number` | — | Gap between items in px |\n| `lanes` | `number` | `1` | Lanes for masonry layouts |\n| `initialOffset` | `number \\| (() => number)` | — | Scroll offset (px) for the server slice — server-render at a scroll position (deep link / restore). Element only; see [SSR](#ssr) |\n| `initialRect` | `{ width: number; height: number }` | — | Viewport hint for a server-rendered slice (SSR). When set, the server paints the initial visible rows; omit for client-only fill. See [SSR](#ssr). |\n| `getItemKey` | `(index: number) => number \\| string \\| bigint` | the index | Stable per-item identity so cached measurements survive reorder |\n| `rangeExtractor` | `(range: Range) => number[]` | `defaultRangeExtractor` | Hook over the visible range: force extra indexes (e.g. a pinned sticky header) into the rendered window. Compose with `defaultRangeExtractor` from `@tanstack/virtual-core` |\n| `indexAttribute` | `string` | `'data-index'` | DOM attribute carrying the item index for `measureElement`. Give two instances measuring the same element (a grid cell) distinct attributes |\n| `initialMeasurementsCache` | `VirtualItem[]` | — | Pre-measured items (plain data) to seed the measurement cache |\n| `anchorTo` | `'start' \\| 'end'` | `'start'` | Anchor the window to the list end (a chat pinned to newest). Client-behavioral: it does not position the server slice — use `initialOffset` for that |\n| `followOnAppend` | `boolean \\| ScrollBehavior` | `false` | With `anchorTo=\"end\"`: stay pinned to the end as items append |\n| `scrollEndThreshold` | `number` | `1` | How close (px) to the end still counts as \"at the end\" |\n| `scrollMargin` | `number` | `0` | The list's offset (px) from the top of its scroll area, when other content sits above it in the same scroller. `item.start` values then INCLUDE this margin — subtract it when positioning items relative to the list (see the window example) |\n| `enabled` | `boolean` | `true` | Disable switch. `false` is not a freeze: the virtualizer unobserves, clears its measurements, and renders an empty window until re-enabled |\n| `isRtl` | `boolean` | `false` | Right-to-left horizontal lists |\n| `isScrollingResetDelay` | `number` | `150` | ms after the last scroll event before \"user is scrolling\" ends |\n| `useScrollendEvent` | `boolean` | `false` | Use the native `scrollend` event instead of the `isScrollingResetDelay` timer |\n| `useAnimationFrameWithResizeObserver` | `boolean` | `false` | Batch ResizeObserver measurements into animation frames (avoids \"ResizeObserver loop\" console errors under heavy resize load) |\n| `laneAssignmentMode` | `'estimate' \\| 'measured'` | `'estimate'` | Masonry/multi-lane: assign items to lanes by estimated or measured sizes |\n| `useCachedMeasurements` | `boolean` | `false` | Make the default measurer return the cached (or estimated) size instead of reading the DOM — freezes item sizes when they are already known |\n| `debug` | `boolean` | `false` | Verbose engine logging |\n| `measureElement` | `(element, entry, instance) => number` | border-box measurer | Replace HOW an item's size is read from its element (e.g. include margins, or measure a child) |\n\n## `<window-virtualizer>` input reference\n\nSame as `<virtualizer>` except `getScrollElement` is not accepted — the scroll element is\nalways `window`. Unlike `<virtualizer>` there are two changed defaults:\n\n- `horizontal` is accepted (the page scrolls sideways) and defaults to `false`.\n- `initialOffset` defaults to the live window scroll position (`window.scrollY`, or\n  `window.scrollX` when `horizontal`) on the client and `0` on the server. Pass a number to\n  override it — e.g. to server-render a slice at a scroll position, paired with\n  `initialRect` (see [SSR](#ssr)).\n\n`scrollMargin` is the signature window-virtualizer option: a window-scrolled list almost never\nstarts at the very top of the page, so pass the list's offset from the top of the document and\nsubtract it from `item.start` when positioning (the window example measures it with\n`offsetTop` on mount).\n\n## Inside your own scroll handler, read the element — not the virtualizer\n\nThe virtualizer attaches its scroll listener in `onMount`; a handler in your markup attaches\nat hydrate, earlier. During any single scroll event your handler therefore runs FIRST, while\nthe virtualizer still holds the PREVIOUS event's offset — so `v.isAtEnd()` and\n`v.getDistanceFromEnd()` called inside your `onScroll` are one event stale (a jump to the top\ncan still report \"at end\"). Compute from the element instead; the arithmetic is identical:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl onScroll() {\n  const el = scrollEl()\n  if (!el) return\n  const atEnd = el.scrollHeight - el.scrollTop - el.clientHeight <= 80\n}>\n```\n\nEverywhere else — click handlers, effects, `<script>` blocks — `v.isAtEnd()` and friends are\ncurrent and safe to use.\n\n## The virtualizer's lifetime must match its scroll element's\n\nDeclare the `<virtualizer>` in the same conditional scope as its scroll element. If the\nscroll container can be unmounted and remounted (an `<if>`, a route transition), put the\ntag inside that same conditional:\n\n```marko\n<if=show>\n  <virtualizer/v count=1000 estimateSize=() => 35 getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()/>\n  <div/scrollEl class=\"list\">...</div>\n</if>\n```\n\nThe tag builds its live virtualizer in `onMount` and re-reads `getScrollElement` only when\none of its inputs changes. A scroll element replaced WITHOUT any input change is invisible\nto the tag — Marko's compile-time reactivity cannot track through the `getScrollElement`\nthunk into your template's scope — so a tag left mounted outside the conditional would stay\nbound to the removed element and render nothing after the remount. Co-locating the tag makes\nits lifecycle follow the element's: unmount tears the instance down, remount builds a fresh\none. (Note: scroll position resets on remount, as a fresh element starts at offset 0.)\n\n## SSR\n\nBoth tags render on the server **without an `<if=mounted>` guard** and build their live, observing\nvirtualizer client-side in `onMount`. There are two modes.\n\n**Client-fill (default).** Without `initialRect` the server renders an empty container; on mount the\nclient measures the scroll element and fills in the visible rows:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl style=\"height: 400px; overflow-y: auto; position: relative;\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=10000\n    estimateSize=() => 35\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  />\n  <div style=`height: ${v.totalSize}px; position: relative`>\n    <for|item| of=v.virtualItems>\n      <div style=`position: absolute; top: 0; width: 100%; height: ${item.size}px; transform: translateY(${item.start}px)`>\n        Row ${item.index}\n      </div>\n    </for>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n**Server slice (`initialRect`).** Pass a viewport hint and the server paints the initial visible\nrows into the HTML, so there is real content on first paint before the client resumes:\n\n```marko\n<virtualizer/v\n  count=people.length\n  estimateSize=() => 48\n  getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n  initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n/>\n```\n\n`initialRect` is a hint, not a measurement: the server has no real viewport, so it uses this size to\ncompute the slice, and the client re-measures the actual scroll element on mount and takes over. The\ninstance built for the slice is transient — nothing live is serialized; only plain data (the item\npositions and total size) crosses and recomputes identically on resume. The full\nfetch → serialize → resume → slice flow is shown in the SSR data-fetching example.\n\n> **Note (no-JS):** a server slice does not by itself make a no-JavaScript page. If the virtualizer\n> sits inside an `<await>` with a placeholder (as in the data-fetching examples), Marko streams the\n> awaited content out of order and reveals it with a small inline script — with JavaScript disabled\n> the painted rows are in the HTML but the page renders blank. Script-free visibility requires\n> in-order rendering (no placeholder).\n\n**Scroll restore (`initialOffset`, element only).** To server-render the list at a scroll position\ninstead of the top — a deep link, or a restored scroll — pass `initialOffset` alongside `initialRect`.\nThe server paints the slice around that offset (it includes `overscan`, so the first *painted* row\nsits a few rows above the first *visible* one). A scroll container's `scrollTop` can't be set\ndeclaratively in HTML, so restore it on the client on mount to line the rows up:\n\n```marko\n<div/scrollEl class=\"list\">\n  <virtualizer/v\n    count=people.length\n    estimateSize=() => 48\n    getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n    initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n    initialOffset=(100 * 48)\n  />\n  <!-- rows … -->\n</div>\n<lifecycle onMount() { const el = scrollEl(); if (el) el.scrollTop = 100 * 48 }/>\n```\n\nFor `<window-virtualizer>` the offset comes from `window.scrollY` (browser scroll restoration), so\n`initialOffset` is not a separate prop there.\n\n### Streaming: the tag inside `<await>`\n\nThe SSR modes above compose with Marko's streaming as-is — place the virtualizer inside an\n`<await>` and everything holds *per streamed chunk*:\n\n```marko\n<try>\n  <@placeholder>\n    <p>Loading people…</p>\n  </@placeholder>\n  <@catch|err|>\n    <p>Failed to load: ${(err as Error).message}</p>\n  </@catch>\n\n  <await|people| value=fetchPeople()>\n    <div/scrollEl class=\"scroll-container\">\n      <virtualizer/v\n        count=people.length\n        estimateSize=() => 48\n        getScrollElement=() => scrollEl()\n        initialRect=({ width: 800, height: 400 })\n      />\n      <!-- sizer + rows exactly as usual -->\n    </div>\n  </await>\n</try>\n```\n\nOn the wire, the server flushes the page shell (with the placeholder) immediately and streams the\nawaited subtree as a **later chunk** once `fetchPeople()` resolves — including the server-painted\nrows when `initialRect` is set. Each streamed chunk **resumes independently**: this list's live\nvirtualizer mounts when its chunk arrives, without waiting for the rest of the page. No extra\nconfiguration — the slice is computed inside the awaited subtree from the resolved data, so the\nserver and the resumed client agree by construction. (The no-JS note above applies: streamed\ncontent is revealed by script.)\n\nThe SSR data-fetching example shows the streamed pattern with client-rendered rows; the\nserver-slice example shows it with server-painted rows — its test suite includes a wire-level\nassertion that the placeholder flushes first and the painted rows arrive in a later chunk.\n"}
